"Neon Breaker is a physics-based arcade game where players control a responsive horizontal paddle to bounce a kinetic ball into patterns of destructible blocks. The core mechanic focuses on calculating bounce angles and timing power-up collection, such as 'Multi-Ball' and 'Laser-Paddle' upgrades. Visually, the game utilizes a high-contrast neon aesthetic with glowing trails and explosive particle effects upon brick impact. The win condition requires the player to clear all blocks in the level while preventing the ball from falling below the paddle. Progression introduces moving obstacles and armored blocks that require multiple hits, increasing the challenge and strategic depth."